{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Dissolving and recovering: a solutions quiz","theme":{"background":"#f4fbff","foreground":"#1d3b4f","font":"Comic Sans MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Dissolving"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"When a solid mixes into a liquid and disappears, leaving a clear mixture called a solution."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1-next","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1n-t","content":"Solution"},{"type":"text","id":"c1n-e","content":"A clear liquid mixture made when a solid has dissolved. The solid is still in it, even though we cannot see it."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which of these will dissolve in water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Sugar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Gravel","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-d","label":"Pebbles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What do we call a clear mixture made when a solid dissolves in a liquid?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A solution","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A suspension","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A mixture of rocks","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Mia drops salt into a glass of water and stirs. The salt disappears. She wants the salt back. What should she do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Boil the water away","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Pour the water into a bowl and wait","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Mia boils the water. Steam rises and the salt is left behind in the glass. Well done, that works."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Mia waits. The water slowly dries up, but the salt is not left in a bowl. She had hoped for a clue, not a bowl of nothing."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"How can you get a dissolved solid back out of a solution?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Evaporate the liquid by heating it","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Add more water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"Stir it harder","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-d","label":"Shake it in a bag","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which solid will NOT dissolve in water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Salt","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Sugar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-d","label":"Baking soda","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Jun has salty water. Which way gets the salt back?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Let the water evaporate","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Pour it through a sieve","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Add a magnet","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Is a solution clear or cloudy?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Clear","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Cloudy","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Coloured with bits","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done: you now know about solutions!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You learned how solids dissolve, what a solution is, and how to recover a dissolved solid by evaporating the liquid."}],"actions":[]}}
